output:
[review by LucieFaire]
minor nits and test improv, otherwise good!

---

src/modules/billing/routes/billing.service.ts:165
This fires on every call, and `listOfferedPaymentLinks` is hit by both endpoints (`getSpacePaymentLinks` and `createCheckoutUrl`'s 403 gate), so one mistagged link produces an error log per `GET /payment-links` and per `POST /checkout-url`, indefinitely. What it reports is a static property of the general catalog, a single shared cached key (`billing_payment_links`, `billing-api.service.ts:162`), so we're logging at request cadence a fact that changes once per TTL, at the level that trips error rate alerting. The request itself succeeds; it's an operational misconfiguration to fix in Stripe, which is what `warn` is for and what the repo uses elsewhere for upstream data inconsistencies.

---

src/modules/billing/domain/payment-link-offer.rules.ts:61
 A never-subscribed workspace can only be offered a trial link, and a link only counts as a trial if it carries `trialPeriodDays`. If upstream isn't emitting it yet, every link reads as paid and every new workspace gets an empty catalog plus a 403 on checkout. The unclassified-trial log doesn't cover it either: `isUnclassifiedTrialLink` short-circuits on `isTrialLink`, so a missing `gracePeriod` is logged but a missing `trialPeriodDays` is silent. Worth logging when the general catalog yields zero offers for a space that has never subscribed, and confirming the deploy order against the billing service.

---

src/modules/billing/domain/payment-link-offer.rules.ts:65
`activePlanName` reads `ACTIVE_SUBSCRIPTION_STATUSES` (`subscriptions.repository.ts:61`), which is `['active', 'trialing']`, so a workspace trialing "Pro" has the paid Pro link excluded here and 403s on checkout for it. Grace periods carry no card, so they never auto convert: every pre-enforcement workspace that wants to stay on its plan when the 2 month grace ends has to go through checkout, and this is the link that hides it. 

---

src/modules/entitlements/domain/subscriptions.repository.ts:59
**Nit:** `hasEverSubscribed` counts every status, so an `incomplete_expired` row (initial payment never succeeded, no money moved) permanently turns trials off for the workspace, with no way back since those rows stay as history. Reachable via a negotiated space specific link whose card bounces: a pre-enforcement workspace silently loses its 2 month grace. `canceled`/`past_due`/`unpaid` are right to count; `incomplete_expired` looks like the wrong one. 

